  "prefLabel": "En 804.03 Training of Locators",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "En 804.03 Training of Locators.\n\n(a) Locators shall be trained in accordance with the National Utility Locating Contractors Association (NULCA) Professional Competence Standards for Locating Technicians, Fifth Edition 2017, available as noted in Appendix B, including the competencies as described in (b) below.\n\n(b) If not already specifically included in the above, training programs for locators shall be supplemented to include the following competencies:\n\n(1) Electromagnetic locating;\n\n(2) Instruction in the use of transmitters and receivers;\n\n(3) Procedures for marking underground facilities;\n\n(4) Training in the identification of facilities;\n\n(5) Safety procedures;\n\n(6) Operator map and record reading; and\n\n(7) Familiarity with the rules in this chapter.\n\nSource. #14062, eff 8-21-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/en800.html"
